f. | Termination by franchisor with cause | 16 | We may terminate the franchise agreement if you are in default as outlined in this document and the Franchise Agreement.

g. | "Cause" defined – curable defaults | 16(B) and 16(C) | You have 10 calendar days to cure monetary defaults, and 30 calendar days to cure all other defaults, except non-curable defaults. We reserve the right to limit your access to the WINnovation Platform, Confidential Information, and any other aspects of the WIN Business upon providing you notice of default under Section 16(B) and 16(C) of the Franchise Agreement.

h. | "Cause" defined - non-curable defaults. | 16(A) | The following actions (or failures to act) will constitute non-curable defaults under this Agreement. 

We may terminate this Agreement immediately and without providing prior notice if you are:
subject to voluntary or involuntary bankruptcy or insolvency; or
beginning or in the process of dissolution or receivership or similar action.

We may terminate the Agreement by providing written notice if you engage in any of the following:

